### ⚑⚑ THE SHIPPED sides-1-3 CATALOG IS INCOMPLETE — 203 MISSING TILINGS AT k=2

  OLD (run-k2-regular-scaled-123, the input the scaled shelf ships from):  k=1 90, k=2 265  = 355
  NEW (2026-08-12, current solver):                                        k=1 90, k=2 468  = 558

Two variables changed between them (solver version, and depth-2 sharding), so both were isolated:
  current solver, D2=1  -> 90 / 468 = 558   (identical to D2=16, so depth-2 is NOT the cause)
  union re-prune of OLD raw + NEW raw -> 90 / 468 = 558   (identical to NEW alone)
The union test is the authoritative one: OLD contributes no class NEW lacks, i.e. OLD is a strict
SUBSET of NEW. The old catalog lost 203 k=2 tilings, 43% of the true count.

Cause: this palette's side-3 tiles carry a period-3 angle word, so BUCKET_OK is false, and before the
2026-08-08 4-bucket union the dynamic face-closure filter ran WITHOUT its BUCKET_OK guard and was
unsound on exactly this kind of palette (NOTES 2026-08-08). It deleted vertex types a real tiling
used. regular-doubled was immune (all tiles period <= 2, BUCKET_OK true), which is why its k=1..4
reproduced byte-for-byte earlier today while this palette did not.

CONSEQUENCE: public/reference-atlas-scaled.json ships side-3 tilings derived from the 355-cell file.
The sides-1-2 subclass is unaffected. The k<=7 shelf build running at the time was ALSO reading the
stale 355-cell file, so it was killed rather than allowed to bake the gap in.

